{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And You, a shield</b> — it is a noun and not a verb, for it ought to have been on the pattern of הנני מסב. (n: Ibn Ezra notes that if ואתה were functioning as a verb meaning 'and I shall shield,' its form should match the paradigm הנני מסב, which shows first-person singular progressive/participial conjugation; since it does not, מגן here is a noun.)" "<b>And the meaning of 'a shield'</b> — that He does not come with war." "<b>And the meaning of 'my glory'</b> — for everyone who triumphs has glory."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:59.645443678Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}